WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.714
Here the whole word fades in together.

2
00:00:02.714 --> 00:00:07.000
It works, but it feels flat, because nothing leads your eye.

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:11.487
Now each letter starts a fraction of a second after the one before it.

4
00:00:11.487 --> 00:00:13.090
This is called a stagger.

5
00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:13.667
Around 0.

6
00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:14.179
05 to 0.

7
00:00:14.179 --> 00:00:17.000
1 seconds per letter reads as a smooth wave.

8
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.325
Another option is a mask.

9
00:00:18.325 --> 00:00:21.662
The text sits still while a window slides open and uncovers it.

10
00:00:21.662 --> 00:00:25.000
Combine the mask with a small slide and the reveal feels crisp.

11
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.448
When there is more than one word, bring them in the order people read.

12
00:00:28.448 --> 00:00:30.369
Then hold each line still for a moment.

13
00:00:30.369 --> 00:00:35.000
A good rule of thumb is about a quarter of a second per word, plus a beat, before it moves on.
